  "paged_input_trace_and_arena_fix": {
    "first_loss_point": "src/compiler/vm_emit.mncs::parse_byte_seq_vm_type expected scalar `byte` immediately after `[`, and `VmType` lacked inner sequence bound fields, causing error_code 4 on `pages: [[byte; up_to 32]; up_to 4]` while canonical mncs-vm (`BodyType::Sequence { element: Box<BodyType>, bound }`) already represented nested sequences natively.",
    "scalar_elem_fix": "decl.scalar_sem handles only 2-3 char integer spellings (`u8`..`u64`/`i8`..`i64`); added parse_scalar_elem_vm_type dispatching decl.scalar_kind first for `byte`/`bool`/`u64`/`i64`.",
    "jit_arena_exhaustion_fix": "During lexer::next_token_global<4,32> lowering, 7 linear search loops in vm_emit.mncs (lookup_vm_value_type, find_ssa_block_by_id, find_vm_block_by_id, find_inst_of_kind_in_list, find_vm_record_type, find_vm_record_field, find_vm_record_field_at, find_vm_fn_by_spec, id_in_list) carried full 600B-1.1KB result structs per miss step, exhausting the 1 GiB bump-only Cranelift JIT canonical arena. Refactoring them to carry only the list tail pointer (`rest`) eliminated per-step bump allocations and unblocked next_token_global<4,32>, significant_global<4,32>, scan_header_global<4,32>, and header_global<4,32>."
  },
